# Git stores LF. This repository is edited on Windows, where the default is to write CRLF, and the
# mismatch made every patch script that rewrote a file report thousands of changed lines when it had
# changed three. The rule below is what stops that: the worktree may use either ending, the object
# database always has LF, and a diff shows the edit rather than the line-ending noise.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Archives a release publishes carry whatever the platform expects, so they are left alone.
*.zip binary
*.tar.gz binary
